.TH MONCTL 1 "2026-11-19" "monctl 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
monctl \- monitor control: profiles, per-game profiles, brightness and MSI settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B monctl
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B monctl
controls every connected monitor: brightness, contrast and input over DDC/CI through
.BR ddcutil (1),
and the on-screen settings of MSI monitors (game mode, Night Vision, smart crosshair, response time,
Eye Saver) over USB through
.BR msigd .
Profiles store the settings of all monitors at once. They can be applied by hand, automatically while
a game or another program runs, at times of day, or from global keyboard shortcuts in the tray.
.PP
.I MONITOR
is an index from
.BR "monctl list" ,
a monitor key such as
.BR MAG323UPF ,
a connector such as
.BR DP-3 ,
or
.BR all .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List the monitors and how each one is controlled.
.TP
.BR status " [\fIMONITOR\fR] [" \-\-all "] [" \-\-json ]
Show settings. \fB\-\-all\fR includes every setting msigd reports.
.TP
.BI set " MONITOR KEY" = VALUE " \fR..."
Change settings, for example \fBmonctl set MAG323UPF game_mode=fps night_vision=ai\fR or
\fBmonctl set VX3418-2KPC input=hdmi1\fR. Values are checked before anything is sent; settings that can
disconnect or hang a monitor over USB are refused.
.TP
.BI brightness " LEVEL" " \fR[\fIMONITOR\fR]"
Set brightness (0\-100). Without a monitor, or with \fBall\fR, brightness matching applies (see \fBrange\fR).
.TP
.BR range " [\fIKEY LOW HIGH\fR | \fIKEY\fR " reset ]
Brightness matching: the range a monitor uses for the "all monitors" level, so different panels look
alike. Without arguments, list the ranges.
.TP
.BR schedule " [" list " | " add " \fIHH:MM PROFILE\fR | " remove " \fIHH:MM\fR]"
Apply a profile when a time of day passes, also when it passed while the computer slept. After a game
exits, automatic profiles return to the profile scheduled for that time.
.TP
.BR profile " " list " | " show " | " save " | " apply " | " delete " \fINAME\fR"
Manage profiles. \fBsave\fR stores the current settings of all connected monitors.
.TP
.BR auto " [" list " | " on " | " off " | " default " \fIPROFILE\fR | " add " \fIMATCH PROFILE\fR [" \-\-focused "] | " remove " \fIMATCH\fR | " procs " | " games ]
Automatic profiles. \fIMATCH\fR is a process name (case-insensitive, \fB.exe\fR optional), \fBsteam:game\fR
for any Steam game, or \fBsteam:\fIAPPID\fR for one game (\fBauto games\fR lists them). The first matching
rule wins; when the last matching program exits, the scheduled or default profile is applied.
\fB\-\-focused\fR makes a rule apply only while the program's window has focus (KDE Plasma).
\fBprocs\fR lists running processes.
.TP
.BR watch " [" \-\-interval " \fISECONDS\fR]"
Apply automatic profiles and the schedule without the tray.
.TP
.BR config " [" msigd " [\fIPATH\fR]]"
Show monctl's settings, or set the path of the msigd binary.
.TP
.BR tray " [" \-\-window ]
Run the tray icon (needs PyQt6). The tray offers profiles, brightness, MSI settings, inputs,
automatic profiles, global keyboard shortcuts and starting at login.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/monctl/profiles.json
Saved profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.config/monctl/settings.json
Automatic-profile rules, schedule, brightness ranges and other settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/monctl/tray.log
Unexpected errors in the tray.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/monctl/
Input lists read from monitors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MONCTL_MSIGD
Path of the msigd binary, if it is not on \fBPATH\fR.
.TP
.B MONCTL_STEAM_ROOT
Steam directory, if it is not in a standard place.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
monctl profile save Gaming
monctl auto add steam:game Gaming
monctl auto default Desktop
monctl auto on
monctl schedule add 21:00 Night
monctl range U28E590 0 80
monctl brightness 40
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ddcutil (1),
.B msigd
(https://github.com/doodersrage/msigd)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/doodersrage/monctl/issues
